<title>USA: Registry buys consulting provider Shamrock.</title>
<headline>Registry buys consulting provider Shamrock.</headline>
<dateline>NEWTON, Mass. 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Registry Inc said it bought privately held computer consulting service provider Shamrock Computer Resources Ltd for about $45.5 million in stock.</p>
<p>Minneapolis-based Shamrock will report earnings of about $3.5 million in fiscal 1996 on revenue of about $38.5 million, Registry said.</p>
<p>Registry did not say how much the acquisition would add to its own earnings per share.</p>
<p>Registry officials were not immediately available to comment.</p>
</text>
